po"><addressbook><name>TAMAGAWA YASUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAGAWA, YASUHISA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMAGAWA YASUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAGAWA, YASUHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An infrared optical system for an infrared camera comprises a support member for holding a convex lens composed of low-dispersion material that transmits infrared rays. A diaphragm for controlling the light entering the convex lens is arranged in front of the convex lens. An aberration corrector for decreasing spherical aberration is provided near the diaphragm. In addition, behind the convex lens is arranged a plate for field smoothing, whose thickness varies with the height of the image so that the curvature of field can be canceled.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un système optique à infrarouges pour caméra à infrarouges comprenant un élément support qui maintient une lentille faite d'un matériau à faible dispersion transmettant le rayonnement infrarouge. A l'avant de la lentille convexe est disposé un diaphragme qui règle la lumière traversant ladite lentille. Près du diaphragme se trouve un correcteur d'aberrations qui atténue les déformations sphériques. Derrière la lentille convexe, on trouve en outre une plaque de lissage de champ dont l'épaisseur varie en fonction de la hauteur de l'image de manière à supprimer la courbure du champ.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>